{
  "slug": "harness-designing-plugin",
  "name": "Harness Designing Plugin",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Harness Designing Plugin helps design teams turn their scattered AI setup — Notion prompts, Figma comments, AGENTS.md rules, chat histories — into a five-layer design harness that compounds across sessions and rotations.\n\nFour skills walk you through the assembly:\n• /hd:learn — Q&A about the five-layer concept (Context Engineering, Skill Curation, Workflow Orchestration, Rubric Setting, Knowledge Compounding)\n• /hd:setup — detects existing harness artifacts, pre-analyzes all five layers in parallel (5× harness-auditor + rubric-recommender), then walks you through link / critique / scaffold / skip per layer\n• /hd:maintain — captures lessons and promotes them to team rules in AGENTS.md with SHA-256 plan-hash proof-of-consent\n• /hd:review — audits harness health in a 2-batch parallel dispatch (5 layer-specialist agents + 2–3 context agents); critiques harness artifacts against quality rubrics\n\nShips 9 sub-agents and 14 starter rubrics (distilled from pbakaus/impeccable, Nielsen's 10 heuristics, Material 3, Fluent 2). Each rubric carries a Scope & Grounding section with personas, user stories, realistic scenarios, and anti-scenarios. Validated across a six-repo pilot matrix.\n\nThis plug-in is the companion toolkit to Bill Guo's Substack series on design harnessing. Structural inspiration: EveryInc/compound-engineering-plugin.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **4 skills**, **3 agents** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (4): `hd-learn` (Answers questions about the five-layer design harness framework), `hd-maintain` (Captures design lessons and proposes rule adoptions from narrative to rule), `hd-review` (Reviews harness health (full) or targets one layer/file (targeted)), `hd-setup` (Walks the five-layer design harness layer by layer)\n- **Agents** (3): `analysis`, `research`, `review`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `context7`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install harness-designing-plugin@claude-community` from `BilLogic/harness-designing-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 4,
    "agent": 3,
    "mcp": 1
  },
